#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1260.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199261} :activity/id #uuid "a0472270-5f40-5310-8129-ab5eb91d56d0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048585 :topic/id #uuid "abbe9530-902a-5d99-8c65-74734dada530" :topic/math-academy-id 4173} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199261 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199457 :tutorial/content "Recall that the moments of inertia $I_x$ and $I_y$ of a thin plate $D$ about the $x$- and $y$- axes are given by\n\n$$\nI_x = \\iint\\limits_D y^2\\,\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm dA \\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\nI_y = \\iint\\limits_D x^2\\,\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm dA,\n$$\n\nwhere the factors $y^2$ and $x^2$ represent the squared distances from a point on the plate to the $x$- and $y$-axes, respectively.\n\nIn general, the **moment of inertia about an axis $l$** of a plane lamina occupying the region $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda(x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the point $(x,y)$ to the axis $l.$\n\nFor example, consider the thin plate that occupies the region\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -1 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwith mass density function $\\lambda(x,y) = 3x+6.$ Let's find its moment of inertia about the line $y=2.$\n\n![](images/24/2451a992f9ecdea8aa1775b64b3a182e0df3f7eab8cac87307c49ed164c6b813.png)\n\nThe distance between a point $(x,y)$ on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |2 - y|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(3x+6)\\,|2-y{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}3(x+2)(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+2)\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}3(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{2}]}_{-1}^{1}\\cdot [(y-2)^{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-1+8) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "a69630f6-6774-5350-b275-26cd501135dc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5070 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "a7b5aafb-1437-5b53-ac08-026c4b750ce9" :step/math-academy-id 31760 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199342}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199342 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198415 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198057 :question/id #uuid "985e1b18-0023-55ba-b4e4-69a109d8de58" :question/math-academy-id "e-12485"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049331} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050409}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198644} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198646} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235555} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281669} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281671} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281674} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281675} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281679} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372223} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429803} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429804}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"} :step/id #uuid "30041ef5-a8d3-542d-8b3b-ca183a630d86" :step/math-academy-id 44957 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199343}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199343 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198416 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198058 :question/id #uuid "eab955a5-019b-5219-b5d5-32e3818be4b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-12486"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198647} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198648} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284384} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284385} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284386} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284387} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372230} {:db/id #edb/r